Story: Learning with self-levelling
  As a pilot learning to fly
  I want the plane to level itself when I let go of the sticks
  So that I can learn the controls without it getting away from me

  In [[ANGLE]], the plane levels its wings when you release the sticks. Thus the plane stays
  under control while you learn. In this tutorial, you select ANGLE, throw the plane and roll
  it. Then you release the stick, and the wings become level again. The VTOL has the same
  help in FBWA: see [[Flying a VTOL with self-levelling]].

  Scenario: Pick ANGLE mode and throw
    When the pilot changes flight mode
    Then the flight mode is ANGLE
    When the pilot throws the plane with the throttle
    Then the plane is flying
    When the pilot rolls the plane to the left
    Then the wings are banked
    When the pilot releases the roll stick
    Then the wings are level
